ENGINE_LOADED(5009,{"ws":5009,"brand":"Sol Health","study":{"id":10692,"name":"Sol Health insight engine 90D","created":true,"window":["2026-07-17","2026-10-15"]},"pillars":[{"id":"p1","name":"Depth over surface connection","name_zh":"深度连接，而非表面关系","verdict":"owned","headline":"Isolation thrives in the shadows of superficiality.","headline_zh":"孤独，藏在浮于表面的关系里。","territory":"Loneliness inside relationships and the wish for connection that holds through discomfort. Sol already leads here: 24 of its 37 clustered organic posts sit in this theme, against 37 of 176 for BetterHelp and Talkspace combined.","territory_zh":"关系中的孤独，以及渴望一种经得起不适的真实连接。Sol 已在此领先：其 37 条被聚类的自然帖子中有 24 条属于该主题，而 BetterHelp 与 Talkspace 合计 176 条中仅有 37 条。","persona":{"themeId":79616,"title":"The Resilient Nurturer","characterId":2868,"characterName":"Livia Hartwell","summary":"Self-care and growth focused; prefers deep, authentic ties over superficial ones; seeks understanding, validation and community. Sol's strongest persona (28 posts).","created":true},"tension":{"themeId":79618,"type":"pain_points","title":"Navigating Emotional Challenges in Relationships and Mental Health","summary":"Keeping authentic connection is hard: feeling overlooked, fear of judgment, pressure to mask vulnerability, loneliness, and difficulty starting honest conversations."},"angle":{"id":23735,"type":"psychological","title":"Isolation Due to Superficial Connections","text":"Attachment Theory: in a digital world many relationships stay on the surface; without secure, deep connection people feel lonely and isolated even when surrounded by others.","created":true},"story":{"id":3722,"title":"Isolation thrives in the shadows of superficiality.","narrative":"Livia Hartwell, who runs community wellbeing workshops, notices conversations shrinking to emojis and texts that feel hollow. Seeing a gathering she was not part of, she realises she has built an illusion of connection. She shares her own struggle, others answer with theirs, and she learns that depth takes vulnerability, patience and spaces where the masks can come off.","created":true},"propositions":[{"id":5280,"itemId":22447,"type":"usp","title":"From Loneliness to Connection","text":"Sol Health Therapy matches you with a therapist who both understands and relates to your journey, helping you foster deeper connections. Tagline: \"Transition from Loneliness to Meaningful Connections with Sol Health.\"","created":true},{"id":5279,"itemId":22441,"type":"rtb","title":"Find your voice within the noise of superficiality","text":"Our rigorous training ensures you receive expert guidance tailored to your unique experiences. Tagline: \"Speak your truth and build connections that matter.\"","created":true},{"id":5278,"itemId":22435,"type":"product_features","title":"From Shadows to Substance: Therapy That Values You","text":"For just $30 per session, Sol Health connects you with a therapist who truly understands you. Tagline: \"Illuminate your path to authentic connections with Sol Health.\"","created":true}],"kpi":{"evidencePosts":61,"engagement":159113,"brandPosts":24,"brandEng":102964},"sov":{"brandShare":64.9,"categoryShare":21.0,"brandPosts":24,"brandTotal":37,"catPosts":37,"catTotal":176},"trend":{"months":["2026-07","2026-08","2026-09","2026-10"],"brand":[2,11,7,4],"category":[10,17,8,2]},"trendNote":"Organic posts per month in SOMIN cluster 79618 (posts-aggregate with clusterIds and a PROFILE breakdown; brand = Sol Health, category = BetterHelp + Talkspace). July covers 17-31 Jul and October 1-15 Oct only, matching the study window, so both are partial months.","examples":{"tofu":[{"postId":683108195,"src":"organic","net":"instagram","date":"2026-09-04","img":"e683108195","text":"Real connection asks something of us that an algorithm never will: the willingness to stay when it gets uncomfortable. So much of what we call closeness now is frictionless by design, and somewhere in the smoothness we’ve lost the muscle for the harder, realer thing.\nEvery relationship that…","metrics":{"likes":64480,"comments":83,"shares":null,"views":null},"score":{"bucket":"ABOVE_AVERAGE","conf":0.827},"why":"Sol's most-engaged post in the window (64.5k likes): a rupture-and-repair carousel that frames therapy as a place to practise staying connected.","why_zh":"Sol 本期互动最高的帖子（6.45 万赞）：以\"破裂与修复\"为主题的轮播图，把心理咨询诠释为练习保持连接的地方。"},{"postId":683108199,"src":"organic","net":"instagram","date":"2026-08-30","img":"e683108199","text":"Loneliness is the absence of connection and not feeling met, not company.\n° Cathy, therapist at Sol","metrics":{"likes":null,"comments":4,"shares":38,"views":null},"score":{"bucket":"ABOVE_AVERAGE","conf":0.803},"why":"Therapist Cathy reframes loneliness as not feeling met rather than being alone, which is exactly the tension this pillar targets.","why_zh":"咨询师 Cathy 指出孤独不是没人陪，而是没有被真正回应，正中本支柱的核心张力。"},{"postId":683108201,"src":"organic","net":"instagram","date":"2026-08-28","img":"e683108201","text":"Emotional loneliness inside a relationship can feel even emptier than being alone. Companionship without real closeness often becomes coexistence, and over time, that can quietly erode your spirit.\n° Cathy, therapist at Sol","metrics":{"likes":13175,"comments":79,"shares":3454,"views":304725},"score":null,"why":"Loneliness inside a relationship drew 305k views and 3.5k shares; SOMIN clickability confidence is under 0.80, so no score is shown.","why_zh":"\"关系中的孤独\"获得 30.5 万次播放、3,454 次分享；SOMIN 点击率预测置信度低于 0.80，因此不显示分数。"}],"mofu":[{"postId":683108211,"src":"organic","net":"instagram","date":"2026-08-13","img":"e683108211","text":"Healing happens in relationship. Human beings regulate in the presence of one another. A body that has spent months braced and unsettled comes back to itself not through information, but through steadiness, the felt sense of another person staying. We have become skilled at functioning and less…","metrics":{"likes":null,"comments":0,"shares":null,"views":null},"score":{"bucket":"ABOVE_AVERAGE","conf":0.868},"why":"Explains Sol's care model: meeting people in their own language and holding the whole person, with no hard call to action.","why_zh":"阐述 Sol 的服务理念：用对方自己的语言沟通、照顾完整的人，没有硬性转化引导。"},{"postId":683108185,"src":"organic","net":"instagram","date":"2026-09-14","img":"e683108185","text":"A BRIEF INQUIRY INTO BEING SEEN\nWe rarely have the clinical words for what we’re carrying. We don’t say we’re experiencing anhedonia or depression; we say we feel off, we feel nothing, we don’t feel like ourselves. So much of what weighs on us was never meant to be labeled or triaged: the…","metrics":{"likes":null,"comments":1,"shares":null,"views":null},"score":null,"why":"Makes the evidence case that the therapeutic relationship itself predicts real change, lending credibility to the connection story.","why_zh":"用研究依据说明\"咨询关系本身\"最能预测改变，为连接叙事提供可信度。"},{"postId":683108139,"src":"organic","net":"instagram","date":"2026-09-24","img":"e683108139","text":"Holistic is a partnership with your nervous system.\nOur lives are made up of all of our parts: relational, emotional, physical, mental, spiritual, and none of them exists or grows in isolation from the others. So wherever you find yourself on your own unique node of the human journey, all of you…","metrics":{"likes":null,"comments":0,"shares":5,"views":null},"score":null,"why":"Explains Sol's holistic approach, holding relational, emotional, physical, mental and spiritual parts together.","why_zh":"解释 Sol 的整体疗愈方式：同时照顾关系、情绪、身体、心理与精神层面。"}],"bofu":[{"postId":683188493,"src":"paid","net":"instagram","date":"2026-09-29","img":"ea683188493","text":"Therapists who understand modern dating, breakups, and relationships that just don't feel right.","metrics":{"likes":null,"comments":null,"shares":null,"views":null},"score":{"bucket":"AVERAGE","conf":0.977},"why":"Paid Instagram/Threads ad (29 Sep - 8 Oct): on-image hook \"Breakups Are Exhausting.\" plus the $30 per session, no-insurance offer and a See details button.","why_zh":"Instagram/Threads 付费广告（9 月 29 日至 10 月 8 日）：画面文案\"分手让人筋疲力尽\"，配合每次 30 美元、无需保险的优惠及\"查看详情\"按钮。"},{"postId":683188486,"src":"paid","net":"instagram","date":"2026-09-29","img":"ea683188486","text":"What was the hardest part of your breakup?\nPersonalized, holistic therapy for $30 per session.\nIntroducing a modern therapy experience called Sol. \nGet matched to therapists who understand breakups, modern dating and relationships, and the weight of it all.","metrics":{"likes":null,"comments":null,"shares":null,"views":null},"score":null,"why":"Same $30 per session offer opened with a breakup question and a short-film cover; Ads Library has no engagement data and the score is under the gate.","why_zh":"同样的每次 30 美元优惠，以\"分手最难的部分\"提问和短片封面开场；广告库无互动数据，点击率置信度未过门槛。"}]}},{"id":"p2","name":"Care that gets your culture","name_zh":"懂你文化背景的心理咨询","verdict":"contested","headline":"Silence can be louder than words, especially in the face of stigma.","headline_zh":"在污名面前，沉默往往比言语更响亮。","territory":"Stigma, cost and too few culturally competent therapists keep people from starting therapy. Both competitors post heavily here (63 of 176 posts); Sol has 8 posts, mostly grant and matching content.","territory_zh":"污名、费用以及缺乏具备文化胜任力的咨询师，让很多人迟迟不开始咨询。两家竞品在此大量发声（176 条中占 63 条）；Sol 有 8 条，主要是资助计划与咨询师匹配内容。","persona":{"themeId":79615,"title":"The Empowered Connector","characterId":2867,"characterName":"Amara Kingsley","summary":"Growth- and wellness-minded, community-driven and justice-oriented; wants connection, empowerment and belonging. Sol 8 posts vs Talkspace 31, BetterHelp 12.","created":true},"tension":{"themeId":79620,"type":"pain_points","title":"Breaking the Barriers: Addressing Stigma and Accessibility in Mental Health Support","summary":"Stigma around asking for help, little affordable or culturally competent care, fear of judgment and pressure to look 'perfect'; marginalized communities face extra cultural barriers."},"angle":{"id":23743,"type":"psychological","title":"Cultural Barriers","text":"Cultural Competence Theory: language gaps, cultural misunderstanding and too few culturally competent providers leave people from diverse backgrounds feeling alienated and slow to seek help.","created":true},"story":{"id":3723,"title":"Silence can be louder than words, especially in the face of stigma.","narrative":"At her community center, Amara Kingsley sees how much silence weighs on the people around her. She designs her mental health workshops as warm, open spaces, a refuge from the stigma that keeps neighbours from seeking help, and hopes to start a candid conversation about cultural barriers in care. Unspoken fears stop people reaching out; talking is where the barriers start to fall.","created":true},"propositions":[{"id":5283,"itemId":22461,"type":"usp","title":"Healing starts when you're truly heard.","text":"With Sol Health Therapy, you're matched with a therapist who knows cultural nuances that resonate with you. Tagline: \"Your Experience Matters: Connect with a Therapist Who Listens!\"","created":true},{"id":5282,"itemId":22457,"type":"rtb","title":"Cultural Conversations for Healing Hearts.","text":"Sol Health Therapy connects you with therapists who are not only trained but also culturally adept, ensuring a safe space for your growth. Tagline: \"Heal with understanding, talk with purpose.\"","created":true},{"id":5281,"itemId":22451,"type":"product_features","title":"Affordable Healing: Your Journey Begins with a Conversation","text":"Sol Health's culturally competent therapists are here for you at $30 per session, no insurance necessary. Tagline: \"Conquer your silence, one session at a time.\"","created":true}],"kpi":{"evidencePosts":71,"engagement":74678,"brandPosts":8,"brandEng":12309},"sov":{"brandShare":21.6,"categoryShare":35.8,"brandPosts":8,"brandTotal":37,"catPosts":63,"catTotal":176},"trend":{"months":["2026-07","2026-08","2026-09","2026-10"],"brand":[0,2,5,1],"category":[11,16,29,7]},"trendNote":"Organic posts per month in SOMIN cluster 79620 (posts-aggregate with clusterIds and a PROFILE breakdown; brand = Sol Health, category = BetterHelp + Talkspace). July covers 17-31 Jul and October 1-15 Oct only, matching the study window, so both are partial months.","examples":{"tofu":[{"postId":683108192,"src":"organic","net":"instagram","date":"2026-09-08","img":"e683108192","text":"Go limping. Go with questions. Go while the pieces are still coming together. Don’t wait to be whole. #therapy #mentalhealth","metrics":{"likes":7302,"comments":100,"shares":4458,"views":241493},"score":{"bucket":"AVERAGE","conf":0.853},"why":"'Go limping, don't wait to be whole' challenges the idea that therapy is only for people who are broken; 241k views and 4.5k shares.","why_zh":"\"带着伤也可以出发，不必等到完整\"挑战了\"只有出问题才去咨询\"的观念；24.1 万次播放、4,458 次分享。"},{"postId":683108212,"src":"organic","net":"instagram","date":"2026-08-11","img":"e683108212","text":"bc being a hot mess with a good therapist is kinda chic 🧿🫦🧡","metrics":{"likes":96,"comments":0,"shares":null,"views":null},"score":null,"why":"A playful carousel (\"kinda chic to have attachment issues and impeccable taste\") that makes therapy feel normal rather than shameful.","why_zh":"轻松幽默的轮播图（\"有依恋问题又品味出众，还挺酷\"），让咨询显得平常而非羞耻。"},{"postId":null,"src":"concept","net":null,"date":null,"img":"gen5009_2","text":"Concept render (SOMIN-generated, not published): hands in a knit sweater holding a warm mug by a sunlit window, open notebook on the sill; no face, no text. Made for Sol's planned TikTok 'Don't wait to be whole' about therapy being for the in-between.","metrics":{"likes":null,"comments":null,"shares":null,"views":null},"score":null,"why":"Concept only, with no performance data: a calm visual for the \"you do not have to be falling apart\" message.","why_zh":"仅为概念图，无表现数据：为\"不必等到崩溃才去咨询\"这一信息准备的平静画面。"}],"mofu":[{"postId":null,"src":"concept","net":null,"date":null,"img":"gen5009_1","text":"Concept render (SOMIN-generated, not published): a calm, sunlit therapy room with two armchairs, tea and plants; no people, no text. Made for Sol's planned 'Matched, not sorted' post explaining identity-based matching and anytime rematching.","metrics":{"likes":null,"comments":null,"shares":null,"views":null},"score":null,"why":"None of Sol's 8 posts in this theme explains the service without a price or sign-up CTA, so this concept stands in for the mid-funnel matching explainer.","why_zh":"Sol 在该主题的 8 条帖子都带有价格或报名引导，没有纯讲解服务的中层内容，因此以此概念图代表\"身份匹配\"讲解帖。"}],"bofu":[{"postId":683108178,"src":"organic","net":"instagram","date":"2026-09-15","img":"e683108178","text":"“You should see yourself in whoever is healing with you.”\n@elyse.fox, founder of @sadgirlsclub, on why it mattered to her that Sol’s therapists understand your culture, your background, and the parts of you that usually need explaining.\nThrough the Sol Health x Sad Girls Club grant, get 4 months…","metrics":{"likes":null,"comments":3,"shares":9,"views":null},"score":{"bucket":"ABOVE_AVERAGE","conf":0.826},"why":"Elyse Fox (Sad Girls Club) on seeing yourself in your therapist, tied to a 16-session no-cost grant. The grant closed on 25 Sep.","why_zh":"Sad Girls Club 创始人 Elyse Fox 谈\"在咨询师身上看见自己\"，并推广 16 次免费咨询资助；该资助已于 9 月 25 日截止。"},{"postId":683188483,"src":"paid","net":"instagram","date":"2026-09-29","img":"ea683188483","text":"Go limping. Go with questions. Go while the pieces are still coming together. Don’t wait to be whole. \nPersonalized, holistic therapy for $30 per session.\nIntroducing a modern therapy experience called Sol. \nGet matched to therapists who understand breakups, modern dating, and relationship…","metrics":{"likes":null,"comments":null,"shares":null,"views":null},"score":{"bucket":"AVERAGE","conf":0.832},"why":"Paid version of the 'Go limping' message that adds the $30 per session offer and a See details button (Instagram/Threads, 29 Sep - 8 Oct).","why_zh":"\"带着伤出发\"信息的付费版本，加入每次 30 美元的优惠和\"查看详情\"按钮（Instagram/Threads，9 月 29 日至 10 月 8 日）。"},{"postId":683108194,"src":"organic","net":"instagram","date":"2026-09-13","img":"e683108194","text":"Share this with a man in your life\nMen’s mental health is more important than ego, toxic masculinity, pride, other’s judgement, looking tough, and societal or cultural expectations. \nThat’s why we’re so proud to partner with @blackmenheal, an organization that has spent years removing every…","metrics":{"likes":null,"comments":6,"shares":null,"views":null},"score":{"bucket":"AVERAGE","conf":0.815},"why":"Black Men Heal partnership: 4 months of free, culturally responsive therapy matched on identity, with a direct sign-up link.","why_zh":"与 Black Men Heal 合作：提供 4 个月免费、具文化回应性的咨询，按身份匹配咨询师，并附报名链接。"}]}},{"id":"p3","name":"Worth beyond productivity","name_zh":"价值不止于产出","verdict":"whitespace","headline":"Productivity is a poor substitute for personal peace.","headline_zh":"生产力，替代不了内心的平静。","territory":"The pressure to stay productive, guilt about resting, burnout and comparison. BetterHelp and Talkspace put 49 posts here (83.8k engagement); Sol's 4 posts drew 35 engagements, so the territory is largely open.","territory_zh":"持续高产的压力、休息时的内疚、倦怠与比较。BetterHelp 与 Talkspace 在此发布了 49 条帖子（互动 8.38 万）；Sol 仅 4 条、互动 35 次，这一领域基本空白。","persona":{"themeId":79617,"title":"The Growth Advocate","characterId":2869,"characterName":"Eliott Winters","summary":"Into work culture, healthy living and personal development; wants business success and a balanced life. Small segment (10 posts), none from Sol.","created":true},"tension":{"themeId":79621,"type":"pain_points","title":"Navigating Societal Pressures and Mental Health Challenges","summary":"Internalized self-criticism, the expectation of constant productivity and inadequacy from comparison; burnout and guilt about rest lead to suppressed emotions and neglected needs."},"angle":{"id":23761,"type":"behavioural_economic","title":"Overemphasis on Productivity","text":"Cultural Dimensions Theory: where achievement is prized, people internalize productivity as worth, so falling short brings guilt and inadequacy and their own well-being gets neglected.","created":true},"story":{"id":3724,"title":"Productivity is a poor substitute for personal peace.","narrative":"Eliott Winters coaches companies on healthier work cultures, yet feels his own worth measured in tasks completed and carries guilt whenever he rests. Volunteering with kids who play without needing results, he sees that constant output has cost him belonging and joy, and starts urging clients, and himself, to trade survival-mode productivity for balance and connection.","created":true},"propositions":[{"id":5286,"itemId":22474,"type":"usp","title":"Find Your Balance with Sol Health Therapy.","text":"Experience personalized therapy that respects your unique identity and needs, fostering genuine connection. Tagline: \"Your journey to peace starts with understanding yourself.\"","created":true},{"id":5285,"itemId":22473,"type":"rtb","title":"Put yourself first: Your mental health matters more than your to-do list.","text":"Sol Health provides easy access to qualified therapists focused on aligning mental health with personal values instead of societal metrics. Tagline: \"Prioritize you with Sol Health: Therapy that values your mental peace above all.\"","created":true},{"id":5284,"itemId":22464,"type":"product_features","title":"Rediscover peace beyond productivity.","text":"Sol Health Therapy offers personalized, holistic therapy to help you find balance for just $30 a session, no insurance needed. Tagline: \"Because your mind deserves as much care as your work.\"","created":true}],"kpi":{"evidencePosts":53,"engagement":83871,"brandPosts":4,"brandEng":35},"sov":{"brandShare":10.8,"categoryShare":27.8,"brandPosts":4,"brandTotal":37,"catPosts":49,"catTotal":176},"trend":{"months":["2026-07","2026-08","2026-09","2026-10"],"brand":[0,3,1,0],"category":[8,22,13,6]},"trendNote":"Organic posts per month in SOMIN cluster 79621 (posts-aggregate with clusterIds and a PROFILE breakdown; brand = Sol Health, category = BetterHelp + Talkspace). July covers 17-31 Jul and October 1-15 Oct only, matching the study window, so both are partial months.","examples":{"tofu":[{"postId":683108207,"src":"organic","net":"instagram","date":"2026-08-20","img":"e683108207","text":"High-functioning depression and anxiety.\nThe fire’s still burning. Tend to it.\n° Thaïs, therapist at Sol","metrics":{"likes":null,"comments":0,"shares":4,"views":null},"score":{"bucket":"ABOVE_AVERAGE","conf":0.935},"why":"Therapist Thaïs on high-functioning depression and anxiety: people who look like they are excelling while struggling inside.","why_zh":"咨询师 Thaïs 谈\"高功能抑郁与焦虑\"：外表看似出色，内心却在挣扎。"},{"postId":683108208,"src":"organic","net":"instagram","date":"2026-08-20","img":"e683108208","text":"The optimal human is an illusion.\n° Thaïs, therapist at Sol","metrics":{"likes":null,"comments":0,"shares":3,"views":null},"score":null,"why":"'The optimal human is an illusion': a therapist pushes back on perfection pressure and describes a non-judgmental space.","why_zh":"\"完美的人只是幻觉\"：咨询师反驳完美主义压力，并描述一个不评判的空间。"},{"postId":null,"src":"concept","net":null,"date":null,"img":"gen5009_3","text":"Concept render (SOMIN-generated, not published): a softly glowing carved pumpkin, knit blanket, books and an open journal at dusk; no people, no text. Made for Sol's planned Halloween post about the fear of being 'too much' or 'not enough'.","metrics":{"likes":null,"comments":null,"shares":null,"views":null},"score":null,"why":"Concept only, with no performance data: a seasonal visual for the inadequacy and fear-of-judgment side of this tension.","why_zh":"仅为概念图，无表现数据：为该张力中\"害怕不够好、害怕被评判\"一面准备的节日画面。"}],"mofu":[{"postId":683108167,"src":"organic","net":"instagram","date":"2026-09-21","img":"e683108167","text":"Even the detours feel like alignment when we get clarity on our values.","metrics":{"likes":null,"comments":6,"shares":13,"views":null},"score":{"bucket":"ABOVE_AVERAGE","conf":0.856},"why":"Explains why a 'perfect' life can feel empty and introduces Sol's Values Exercise, a how-to with no direct call to action.","why_zh":"解释为何\"完美\"的生活会让人空虚，并介绍 Sol 的\"价值观练习\"，属于无直接转化引导的方法类内容。"},{"postId":683108206,"src":"organic","net":"instagram","date":"2026-08-21","img":"e683108206","text":"A brief inquiry into loneliness and its universality 🫀","metrics":{"likes":null,"comments":0,"shares":9,"views":null},"score":null,"why":"Two therapists on why loneliness is universal and why sitting with discomfort beats chasing a quick fix.","why_zh":"两位咨询师谈孤独的普遍性，以及为何与不适共处胜过追求速效解决。"}],"bofu":[{"postId":683188488,"src":"paid","net":"instagram","date":"2026-09-29","img":"ea683188488","text":"Therapy built to fit into your life. Affordable, personalized, holistic.","metrics":{"likes":null,"comments":null,"shares":null,"views":null},"score":{"bucket":"AVERAGE","conf":0.905},"why":"Paid ad positioning therapy as something that fits into a busy life (cover: \"signs of chronic anxiety nobody talks about\"), with a See details button.","why_zh":"付费广告把咨询定位为\"能融入忙碌生活\"的服务（封面：\"没人谈论的慢性焦虑信号\"），附\"查看详情\"按钮。"},{"postId":683188478,"src":"paid","net":"instagram","date":"2026-09-30","img":"ea683188478","text":"Personalized, holistic therapy for $30 per session.\nIntroducing a modern therapy experience called Sol.\nGet matched to therapists who understand trauma, relationships, and the messy parts of life.\nYou deserve to feel like yourself again.","metrics":{"likes":null,"comments":null,"shares":null,"views":null},"score":null,"why":"The only Sol creative that names burnout on-image ('Therapy For ... Burnout'), with the $30 per session, no-insurance offer; score under the gate.","why_zh":"唯一在画面中直接点名\"倦怠\"的 Sol 素材，并附每次 30 美元、无需保险的优惠；点击率置信度未过门槛。"}]}}],"created":{"studies":[{"id":10692,"name":"Sol Health insight engine 90D"}],"characters":[{"id":2868,"name":"Livia Hartwell","personaThemeId":79616},{"id":2867,"name":"Amara Kingsley","personaThemeId":79615},{"id":2869,"name":"Eliott Winters","personaThemeId":79617}],"angles":[{"id":23732,"themeId":79618,"used":false},{"id":23733,"themeId":79618,"used":false},{"id":23734,"themeId":79618,"used":false},{"id":23735,"themeId":79618,"used":true},{"id":23736,"themeId":79618,"used":false},{"id":23737,"themeId":79618,"used":false},{"id":23738,"themeId":79618,"used":false},{"id":23739,"themeId":79618,"used":false},{"id":23740,"themeId":79618,"used":false},{"id":23741,"themeId":79618,"used":false},{"id":23742,"themeId":79620,"used":false},{"id":23743,"themeId":79620,"used":true},{"id":23744,"themeId":79620,"used":false},{"id":23745,"themeId":79620,"used":false},{"id":23746,"themeId":79620,"used":false},{"id":23747,"themeId":79620,"used":false},{"id":23748,"themeId":79620,"used":false},{"id":23749,"themeId":79620,"used":false},{"id":23750,"themeId":79620,"used":false},{"id":23751,"themeId":79620,"used":false},{"id":23752,"themeId":79621,"used":false},{"id":23753,"themeId":79621,"used":false},{"id":23754,"themeId":79621,"used":false},{"id":23755,"themeId":79621,"used":false},{"id":23756,"themeId":79621,"used":false},{"id":23757,"themeId":79621,"used":false},{"id":23758,"themeId":79621,"used":false},{"id":23759,"themeId":79621,"used":false},{"id":23760,"themeId":79621,"used":false},{"id":23761,"themeId":79621,"used":true}],"stories":[3722,3723,3724],"products":[{"id":1472,"name":"Sol Health Therapy","profileId":23324}],"propositions":[5278,5279,5280,5281,5282,5283,5284,5285,5286]},"notes":["Workspace 5009 had no studies, stories, products or propositions, so everything in the chain was created in SOMIN this session (ids under \"created\").","Study 10692: organic (PAGES), LAST_90_DAYS = 17 Jul - 15 Oct 2026, all 3 profiles. It clustered 213 of 242 posts: Sol 37, BetterHelp 83, Talkspace 93. Those per-type totals are the SOV denominators (brandTotal 37, catTotal 176). brandShare and categoryShare are percentages (0-100).","KPIs and trends use the study theme metrics and posts-aggregate with clusterIds; the monthly sums reconcile exactly with the study counts for all three themes.","Safety filter (mental-health brand): excluded from examples Sol posts 683275524 and 683275523 (Domestic Violence Awareness Month, hotline), 683108203 (DV hotline), 683108196 and 683108198 (coercive control / power and control), 683108204 and 683108200 (toxic-relationship signs), 683108202 (Meta teen-harm settlement) and 683108214 (\"hope crisis\"), plus ads 683188480/683188482 (cover \"The signs of a toxic relationship you don't see\"). Several sit in P1's cluster 79618 and are among its most engaged, so P1 KPI/SOV figures (study metrics) still include them. Angle 23740 \"Normalization of Toxic Relationships\" was generated but not used.","Score gate: the score is the clickability_score of the image shown (cover image for carousels and DCO ads, thumbnail for reels and video ads); usable only when the top probability > 0.80. 11 of the 19 real (non-concept) examples pass. All others have score null.","posts-search with clusterIds defaults to roughly the last 30 days unless dates are passed; the example search used the study window (17 Jul - 15 Oct).","Paid ads: the study is organic-only, so ads have no cluster; the 5 ads used were matched to pillars by caption and on-image text (verified by opening the images). Ads Library returns no engagement, so ad metrics are null. All 16 Sol ads ran on Instagram + Threads between 29 Sep and 8 Oct. Duplicate creatives (683188494, 683188487, 683188484, 683188489, 683188490/491, 683188479, 683188495, 683246775) were skipped.","Grant posts (Sad Girls Club grant closed 25 Sep; Black Men Heal; a creator scholarship) are historical examples; do not present any grant as currently open.","Concepts gen5009_1/2/3 are existing SOMIN-generated renders (no people, no text, no metrics), copied from img/. The planned captions for gen5009_1 (Matched, not sorted) and gen5009_3 (Halloween) end with a soft \"link in bio\" line; they sit in P2 MOFU and P3 TOFU because of the visual's role (matching explainer, emotional hook). gen5009_4 was not used.","Short stages, left short on purpose rather than padded: P1 BOFU 2, P2 MOFU 1 (concept only, because every Sol post in that theme carries a price or sign-up CTA), P3 MOFU 2, P3 BOFU 2.","Product 1472 uses only SOMIN-detected facts from Sol posts and ads ($30 per session, no insurance needed, identity-based matching, rematching, find-your-match onboarding, therapist training/supervision/mentorship). 9 propositions = 3 stories x (usp, rtb, product_features), each with 5 SOMIN variants; the dashboard shows one variant per proposition (itemId). Variant 22470 (\"pause and reflect anytime\") was skipped as it is not a detected fact.","Story 3723's SOMIN narrative is a single paragraph, so its narrative here is shorter in substance. Persona 79617 (Growth Advocate) is a small segment: 10 posts, none from Sol.","propositions-list paginates over proposition variants (5 per proposition), not propositions; three pages of 20 were needed to read all 9 back."]},{"e683108195":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","e683108199":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","e683108201":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","e683108211":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","e683108185":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","e683108139":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","ea683188493":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","ea683188486":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","e683108192":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","e683108212":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","gen5009_2":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","gen5009_1":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","e683108178":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","ea683188483":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","e683108194":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","e683108207":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","e683108208":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","gen5009_3":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","e683108167":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","e683108206":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","ea683188488":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","ea683188478":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"});
